language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Project assignment: decide how many hours each person works on each project, so that each person's supply and each project's demand are met exactly, within the limits, at minimum total cost.
$ number of people, from the instance supply list
given supply_dim1 : int
$ number of projects, from the instance demand list
given demand_dim1 : int
$ available hours of each person
given supply : matrix indexed by [int(1..supply_dim1)] of int
$ hours required by each project
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..demand_dim1)] of int
$ cost per hour of person i on project j
given cost : matrix indexed by [int(1..supply_dim1), int(1..demand_dim1)] of int
$ the maximum hours person i can contribute to project j
given limit : matrix indexed by [int(1..supply_dim1), int(1..demand_dim1)] of int
$ assign[i,j] is the number of hours person i works on project j
find assign : matrix indexed by [int(1..supply_dim1), int(1..demand_dim1)] of int(0..sum(supply))
$ total_cost is the total cost of all the hours assigned
find total_cost : int(0..sum(supply) * sum(flatten(cost)))
minimising total_cost
such that
$ the total cost is the sum over people and projects of the cost per hour times the hours assigned
total_cost = (sum i : int(1..supply_dim1) . sum j : int(1..demand_dim1) . cost[i,j] * assign[i,j]),
$ the total hours assigned from each person equals that person's supply
forAll i : int(1..supply_dim1) . ((sum j : int(1..demand_dim1) . assign[i,j]) = supply[i]),
$ the total hours assigned to each project equals that project's demand
forAll j : int(1..demand_dim1) . ((sum i : int(1..supply_dim1) . assign[i,j]) = demand[j]),
$ the hours a person contributes to a project do not exceed the limit for that pair
forAll i : int(1..supply_dim1) . forAll j : int(1..demand_dim1) . (assign[i,j] <= limit[i,j])
